## 🎯 What You Can Do Now

### 1. Test the Web App
```bash
# Install http-server if you don't have it
npm install -g http-server

# Serve the built app
http-server dist/

# Or use Node's built-in
npx serve dist/

# Open in browser: http://localhost:8080 or :3000
```

### 2. Build Android APK
```bash
# Sync web assets with Android
npx cap sync

# Build APK
npx cap build android

# Or run on device directly
npx cap run android
```

### 3. Test on Device
```bash
# Install on Android device
adb install dist-debug.apk

# Or use Capacitor
npx cap run android
```

### 4. Prepare for Release
```bash
# Follow BUILD_GUIDE.md or APK_BUILD_CHECKLIST.md
# Key steps:
# 1. Create signing keystore
# 2. Build release APK
# 3. Sign APK
# 4. Align APK
# 5. Upload to Google Play
```

